  "live_records": {
    "q-95603": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95603",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$$\n\n$\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡3=$",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡3 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3+\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3+\\sqrt{9+1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3+\\sqrt{10}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
