    "q-125843": {
      "dom_id": "step-q125843",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$$\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to $\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{2t}),$ for $t>0?$",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{2t}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{2t}+\\sqrt{{(\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{2t})}^{2}+1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{2t}+\\sqrt{\\frac{{t}^{4}-2{t}^{2}+1}{4{t}^{2}}+1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{2t}+\\sqrt{\\frac{{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}+1}{4{t}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{2t}+\\sqrt{{(\\frac{{t}^{2}+1}{2t})}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{2t}+|\\frac{{t}^{2}+1}{2t}|)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $t>0,$ we have $\\frac{{t}^{2}+1}{2t}>0,$ and we can remove the absolute value in the above expression. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{2t}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{2t}+\\frac{{t}^{2}+1}{2t}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2{t}^{2}}{2t}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
