    "q-95612": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95612",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "$$\n\nGiven that $t\\ge 1,$ which of the following is equivalent to $\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡{t}^{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡{t}^{2} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+\\sqrt{{({t}^{2})}^{2}-1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+\\sqrt{{t}^{4}-1}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
