    "q-341486": {
      "dom_id": "step-q341486",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "$$\n\nEvaluate $\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}).$ **Do not round** your answer.\n\n$\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5})=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-1}}$)$",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+x}{1-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5})}{1-(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5})}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}}{1+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\frac{5-\\sqrt{3}}{5}}{\\frac{5+\\sqrt{3}}{5}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,ln\\,(\\frac{5-\\sqrt{3}}{5+\\sqrt{3}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
