    "q-341500": {
      "dom_id": "step-q341500",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "$$\n\nGiven that $-2<w<1,$ express $\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{2w+1}{3})$ using the definition of the inverse hyperbolic tangent.\n\n$\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{2w+1}{3})=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-1}}\n$)$",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+x}{1-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{2w+1}{3}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+\\frac{2w+1}{3}}{1-\\frac{2w+1}{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\frac{3+2w+1}{3}}{\\frac{3-2w-1}{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4+2w}{2-2w}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2+w}{1-w}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
