    "q-341494": {
      "dom_id": "step-q341494",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "$$\n\nGiven that $0<x<\\frac{1}{4},$ express $\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(4\\sqrt{x}-1)$ using the definition of the inverse hyperbolic tangent.\n\n$\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(4\\sqrt{x}-1)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-1}}\n$)$",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+x}{1-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(4\\sqrt{x}-1) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+4\\sqrt{x}-1}{1-4\\sqrt{x}+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4\\sqrt{x}}{2-4\\sqrt{x}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2\\sqrt{x}}{1-2\\sqrt{x}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
          "tag": "mathquill",
          "choices": [],
